23. Window / Rolling Functions

Useful for time series and forecasting.

| Method        | Use                                 | Example                          |
| ------------- | ----------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| `rolling()`   | Moving/window calculations          | `df["Sales"].rolling(7).mean()`  |
| `expanding()` | Expanding calculations              | `df["Sales"].expanding().mean()` |
| `ewm()`       | Exponentially weighted calculations | `df["Sales"].ewm(span=7).mean()` |


====

Example:

df["7_day_average"] = df["Sales"].rolling(7).mean()

Meaning:

Calculate the average Sales over every 7-row window.

